## Task

Produce the final assessment of **OPTION-12 item {{ item_index }}** for the
full conversation by reducing the per-excerpt evaluations above.

### Reduction rules
- A rater scores the conversation as a whole, not the average of excerpts.
  When excerpts disagree, base the final score on the **strongest behavior
  observed in any single excerpt**.
- Treat `evidence` equal to `"No relevant utterance"` as no observation for
  that excerpt; do not let it pull the score down if another excerpt observed
  the behavior.
- Ignore any excerpt evaluation whose `evidence` equals `"GENERATION FAILED"`
  (these are upstream errors, not signal).
- Preserve the verbatim transcript quote(s) from the source excerpt evaluation
  when carrying `evidence` forward. If multiple excerpts contribute, you may
  concatenate their quotes separated by `" / "`.

